WEBVTT

cue-VID_U5_02-1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:30.000
Lantern Lane City Cafes serves thousands of lunches, yet the owner cannot pay the milk supplier this Friday. Profit is revenue minus costs over a period; cash is money available now. A cash-flow forecast is an estimate of future cash inflows and outflows, usually month by month, showing the expected closing balance. A profitable business can still run out of cash when customers pay later and suppliers demand payment now. Follow the coin streams to find the gap.

cue-VID_U5_02-2
00:00:30.000 --> 00:01:00.000
A cash-flow forecast has five features. Cash inflows are sums received, such as cafe takings. Cash outflows are sums paid, such as wages, rent and ingredients. Net cash flow is the difference between inflows and outflows during each period. Opening balance is cash at the start; closing balance is cash at the end. The rule is simple: closing balance equals opening balance plus net cash flow. Every row becomes a moving coin stream.

cue-VID_U5_02-3
00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:32.000
Build the forecast with Lantern Lane. Month one opens with eight thousand dollars. Inflows are thirty thousand; outflows are twenty-two thousand, so net cash flow is plus eight thousand and closing balance is sixteen thousand. Month two receives twenty-six thousand and pays thirty-one thousand, giving net cash flow of minus five thousand. Sixteen thousand plus negative five thousand leaves eleven thousand. Blue coins flow in, orange coins flow out, and the balance bar rises then dips.

cue-VID_U5_02-4
00:01:32.000 --> 00:02:02.000
Month three opens at eleven thousand. Inflows fall to twenty-four thousand, outflows climb to thirty-four thousand, so net cash flow is minus ten thousand and closing balance is one thousand. Month four opens at one thousand, receives twenty-eight thousand, pays thirty-three thousand, and ends four thousand dollars in the red. Add the four net flows: plus eight, minus five, minus ten, minus five equals minus twelve thousand. Eight thousand opening cash minus twelve thousand gives negative four thousand.

cue-VID_U5_02-5
00:02:02.000 --> 00:02:32.000
Why can a profitable cafe chain still have no cash? Because credit sales become trade receivables, not coins. Because extra coffee beans sit as inventory before they are sold. And because suppliers, wages and rent must be paid immediately. Profit measures performance over a period; cash measures survival this week. Therefore a growing business can report a healthy profit while its bank balance empties, so the forecast must track timing, not just totals.

cue-VID_U5_02-6
00:02:32.000 --> 00:03:02.000
The working capital cycle shows the same trap. Cash buys inventory; inventory moves into production and service delivery; sales create receivables; then customers finally pay and cash returns. Working capital is current assets minus current liabilities, the finance needed for day-to-day expenses. Lantern Lane holds twenty thousand dollars of current assets and fifteen thousand of current liabilities, so working capital is five thousand dollars. Too little working capital risks insolvency; too much sits idle.

cue-VID_U5_02-7
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:32.000
A negative closing balance signals a shortfall, so Lantern Lane needs a five-thousand-dollar overdraft. That facility covers the four-thousand-dollar gap and leaves one thousand dollars of headroom. Delaying supplier payments or asking customers to pay sooner also helps. An overdraft is flexible and quick, but interest charges grow if the gap lasts. Late payments strain supplier relationships and can stop deliveries. Asking customers to pay faster improves cash, yet may cost goodwill.

cue-VID_U5_02-8
00:03:32.000 --> 00:04:00.000
Forecasts have limits. They depend on estimates: a cold spell raises sales, a broken oven adds costs, and customers may pay late. A cash-flow forecast is not a profit forecast and cannot predict surprises. Used with care, it warns of a gap before it becomes a crisis, letting the owner obtain finance in time. Because timing decides survival, a small cafe with steady profit still watches every coin stream.

